<!-- OPTION B: SHARED INBOX -->
<div style="background: #f8f9fa; border: 1px solid #ddd; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px; margin: 20px 0;">
<h3 style="color: #333; margin-top: 0;">Option B: Shared Centre Inbox (Microsoft 365)</h3>
<p><em>Choose this if Lineleader emails go to a shared mailbox (like eastgwillimburyonca@codeninjas.com) that multiple staff members access.</em></p>

<p>Shared mailboxes don't support simple forwarding rules, so we'll use <strong>Power Automate</strong> (included free with your Microsoft 365 account).</p>

<h4>Step 1: Open Power Automate</h4>
<ol>
<li>Go to <a href="https://flow.microsoft.com" style="color: #1a73e8;">https://flow.microsoft.com</a></li>
<li>Sign in with your <strong>Microsoft 365 account</strong> (the one that has access to the shared inbox)</li>
</ol>

<h4>Step 2: Create a New Flow</h4>
<ol>
<li>Click <strong>"Create"</strong> in the left menu</li>
<li>Select <strong>"Automated cloud flow"</strong></li>
<li>Name it: ${code("CRM Lead Forwarding")}</li>
<li>Search for the trigger: <strong>"When a new email arrives in a shared mailbox (V2)"</strong></li>
<li>Click <strong>"Create"</strong></li>
</ol>

<h4>Step 3: Configure the Trigger</h4>
<ol>
<li>In <strong>"Original Mailbox Address"</strong>, enter your shared inbox address</li>
<li>Set <strong>"Subject Filter"</strong> to: ${code("New CORE Program Inquiry")}</li>
<li>Under <strong>"Advanced options"</strong>: set <strong>"From"</strong> to: ${code("noreply@lineleader.com")}</li>
</ol>

<h4>Step 4: Add the Forward Action</h4>
<ol>
<li>Click <strong>"+ New step"</strong></li>
<li>Search for: <strong>"Forward an email (V2)"</strong></li>
<li>Set <strong>"Message Id"</strong> to the dynamic value <strong>"Message Id"</strong> from the trigger</li>
<li>Set <strong>"To"</strong> to: ${code(fwdAddr)}</li>
</ol>

<h4>Step 5: Save and Turn On</h4>
